AB  - Over the years, the economic and strategic potential of data has been identified by companies, and nowadays, data has emerged as a valuable digital asset for them. Data can be offered as a product by combining it with a series of services related to data quality, security, trust, communication, and monetization. In this paper, an implementation of Data-as-a-Product (DaaP) developed in Horizon Europe project RE4DY for its use in industrial environments is presented. DaaP is a core concept to enable distributed data management solutions and collaboration among industrial stakeholders. The architecture of the proposed solution consists of core services to enable data abstraction, interoperability, quality, security, and traceability. In addition to them, Data Space components are considered to provide data sovereignty and trust alongside with a Marketplace to promote the discovery of the shared resources. This implementation has been tested in a use case where data from the Swiss Smart Factory was shared with an analytics service provider. The goals of this experiment were to validate the implemented DaaP solution and to perform an initial evaluation of the potential benefits of this concept. The proposed DaaP implementation provides an easy-to-use environment that simplifies the entire workflow for collecting, pre-processing, and sharing data to create data-driven services, and enhances data quality while saving time and reducing costs.
