AB  - This paper presents a concept and implementation of AI-enabled Multi-Agent Systems in service-oriented manufacturing networks. Building on the Asset Administration Shell as a standardized digital representation of assets, product and resource agents were designed to coordinate production processes autonomously, while AI-powered service agents provided additional reasoning capabilities. The approach was validated in a testbed through the production of a customized Multi-Key-Tool. The results show that AI-powered Multi-Agent Systems enable semantic interoperability, decentralized orchestration of processes, and adaptation to customer-specific requirements. At the same time, challenges remain regarding standardized discovery of agents and their assets, cross-company methods, and efficient AI reasoning in real-time shopfloor contexts.
