KW  - Industry 5.0
KW  - Data ecosystems
KW  - Data infrastructures
KW  - Data value chain
AB  - The industrial landscape is evolving toward Industry 5.0, and the massive data contained therein is poised and tasked with unlocking industrial value. Dataspaces are emerging as a sovereign, interoperable, and trusted data circulation environment to harness the data value for the benefit of industrial organizations and citizens. However, existing research on dataspaces has yet to reach a consensus on comprehensively integrating Industry 5.0 value attributes of human-centricity, sustainability, and resilience. Furthermore, there remains a notable gap in referenceable implementation paths and methodologies. To unlock the immense potential of data-driven innovation in the Industry 5.0 era, this paper first introduces the concept of a Dataspace Ecosystem to provide future guidelines. Inspired by this vision, the evolution and derivation of dataspaces are critically reviewed to further conceptualize their novel connotations aligned with Industry 5.0 values. Accordingly, a reference ecosystem model for the dataspace is developed, analyzing the interaction logic of its building block components and core enabling technologies. Then, the application of the dataspace-empowering data value chain is discussed in data lifecycle management and product lifecycle management. Finally, barriers, challenges, and future research directions for the dataspace ecosystem are concluded, respectively. It is expected that this work will be a cornerstone resource for the further development of dataspaces in the Industry 5.0 context, guiding the data-driven industrial journey through this terra incognita.
ER  - 

