AB  - Uncrewed Aerial Vehicles (UAVs) have transformed precision agriculture, enabling high-resolution monitoring of crops, livestock, and soil health. But the lack of open, reproducible workflows and fragmented data sharing limits their potential. The ICAERUS Drone Data Analytics Library (DDAL) addresses this by providing a FAIR-compliant, open-source data space for UAV datasets and analytical models. Built on GitHub, Zenodo, and the ICAERUS Platform, DDAL enables collaborative sharing of raw and processed data, as well as analytical models, across real-world UAV applications including agriculture, forestry, and logistics. At the time of evaluation, DDAL contained 93 models and 144 datasets and had recorded over 11,000 downloads. A contributor survey shows that 81.3% agree DDAL reduces the effort to publish datasets, and 50% would not have shared their data without it. While DDAL aligns with EU open science policies, challenges with quality assurance and sustainability persist. This paper presents DDAL’s design, workflows, and demonstrated impact in opening up data and models for UAV analytics.
