AB  - Interoperable sovereign data and service ecosystems play a pivotal role in shaping digital markets within today’s manufacturing industry. These ecosystems facilitate secure connections among diverse stakeholders across manufacturing supply chains, fostering rapid and seamless communication across organizational boundaries. This connectivity empowers the deployment of services leveraging sensitive process data, allaying concerns about compromising corporate intellectual property. Standardized meta-information, which can be provided in the Asset Administration Shell, plays a critical role in enabling the deployment of these services across different environments. By describing environments in a standardized format, the need for a multitude of input parameters is minimized, streamlining the setup process for these services. Furthermore, adherence to standards like OPC UA ensures compatibility and interoperability, bolstering the efficacy and reliability of the service architecture. This approach not only facilitates efficient deployment of services but also promotes scalability and sustainability within manufacturing ecosystems.
