AB  - Scientific data, as a critical foundational strategic resource, plays a dual role in advancing research and fostering innovation. Against the backdrop of global open science and open data initiatives, as well as China’s policy of recognizing data as a factor of production, this study explores the establishment of a trusted scientific data space for the National Quality Infrastructure (NQI) domain. Specifically, it focuses on the development of an NQI information integration and data sharing platform (NQI IIDSP) led by the National Institute of Metrology, China (NIM). By integrating authoritative data sources, implementing multi-level access control, and standardizing workflows, the platform ensures trusted data governance, facilitates resource interaction, and promotes value co-creation. The platform has preliminarily established a NQI scientific research projects database and the corresponding output database, along with a robust scientific data archiving system (SDAS), laying a solid foundation for the construction of a NQI trusted scientific data space. In the future, efforts will focus on enhancing data resource quality, integrating AI-driven analytics, improving governance mechanisms, and establishing industry standards to support the development of a national integrated data market, ultimately accelerating innovation and digital transformation in the NQI domain.
