AB  - With the advancement of Industry 5.0 and the development of artificial intelligence, enterprises are turning from digitalization to intelligentization. However, in the process of intelligent transformation, enterprises are commonly facing problems such as system interoperability barriers, data silos, and rigid business processes. To address these issues, this study proposes a reference framework for intelligent transformation in the industry. This framework systematically integrates data resource acquisition, data circulation, domain cognitive intelligence construction, and business process reengineering. Theoretically, it establishes an industrial pipeline connecting data acquisition to business optimization through data and knowledge flow. Furthermore, in order to investigate the causal and influence relationships among different factors in the intelligent transformation, we propose an Evidence-grounded Multi-agent Evaluation Methodology (EMEM). This method overcomes the subjectivity and inefficiency of traditional expert scoring by introducing an external knowledge base containing real-world industry practice cases, combined with multi-agent scoring. Based on the scoring process of 12 indicators in 63 real-world industry practice cases, we demonstrate the implementation of this method and validate its effectiveness. Finally, using a case study in the civil aircraft flight test, we demonstrate the application and implementation of the proposed framework, providing a reference blueprint for the industry.
ER  - 

